From: OpenMandriva
Subject: Build fwupd-detect-cet with clang

Meson only builds the CET probe helper when the compiler has the GCC-only
noclone attribute. Clang supports -fcf-protection (and the helper is a
standalone executable of a tiny C main plus an assembly stub), so skip
that check and build whenever -fcf-protection is available on x86_64.

Without this, the daemon logs:
  failed to test CET: Failed to execute child process
  "/usr/libexec/fwupd/fwupd-detect-cet" (No such file or directory)

--- a/plugins/cpu/meson.build
+++ b/plugins/cpu/meson.build
@@ -14,18 +14,10 @@
   dependencies: plugin_deps,
 )
 
-code = '''
-#if !__has_attribute (__noclone__)
-#error symver attribute not supported
-#endif
-static void __attribute__((noinline,noclone)) f(void) {}
-'''
-
-# verify the compiler knows what to do
+# noclone is GCC-only. The helper is a standalone binary (C main + .S stub)
+# compiled with mixed -fcf-protection=full/none; clang can do that.
 if host_cpu == 'x86_64' and cc.has_argument('-fcf-protection')
-  build_fwupdcethelper = cc.compiles(code,
-    name: '__attribute__((noinline,noclone))',
-  )
+  build_fwupdcethelper = true
 else
   build_fwupdcethelper = false
 endif
